name: moving data
boss: DevNull
flavor: Your stderr falls into the void.
brief: wget fetches over http. nc opens a raw tcp connection and hands it to
brief: you as stdin and stdout, which is how you speak any text protocol by
brief: hand. The older ftp and tftp clients are here because the machines you
brief: will meet in a bad week are often older than you are.
brief:
brief: This build of nc can connect out but cannot listen -- server mode is
brief: compiled out on purpose. xos opens no doors it was not asked to.
---
q: download a url to a file named after it
a: wget http://@host@/file.txt
ref: wget
teach: wget
---
q: download a url and save it under a name you choose
a: wget -O out.txt http://@host@/file.txt
ref: wget
teach: wget -O
---
q: download quietly, printing nothing
a: wget -q http://@host@/file.txt
ref: wget
teach: wget -q
---
q: resume an interrupted download rather than starting again
a: wget -c http://@host@/file.txt
ref: wget
teach: wget -c
---
q: check whether a url exists without downloading the body
a: wget --spider http://@host@/file.txt
ref: wget
teach: wget --spider
---
q: download showing the server's response headers
a: wget -S http://@host@/file.txt
ref: wget
teach: wget -S
---
q: send an extra header with the request
a: wget --header 'X-Token: abc' http://@host@/file.txt
ref: wget
teach: wget --header
---
q: post some data rather than fetching
a: wget --post-data 'a=1' http://@host@/submit
ref: wget
teach: wget --post-data
---
q: post the contents of a file
a: wget --post-file @txt@ http://@host@/submit
ref: wget
teach: wget --post-file
---
q: download into a chosen directory
a: wget -P @dir@ http://@host@/file.txt
ref: wget
teach: wget -P
---
q: download claiming to be a particular user agent
a: wget -U xos http://@host@/file.txt
ref: wget
teach: wget -U
---
q: give up if the server has not answered in 10 seconds
a: wget -T 10 http://@host@/file.txt
ref: wget
teach: wget -T
---
q: write the download log to a file instead of the screen
a: wget -o wget.log http://@host@/file.txt
ref: wget
teach: wget -o
---
q: download from https without checking the certificate -- and know why that is bad
a: wget --no-check-certificate https://@host@/file.txt
ref: wget
teach: wget --no-check-certificate
hint: this turns off the only thing proving you are talking to who you think
---
q: open a raw tcp connection to @host@ on port @port@
a: nc @host@ @port@
ref: nc
teach: nc
---
q: speak http by hand -- send a HEAD request through nc
a: printf 'HEAD / HTTP/1.0\r\n\r\n' | nc @host@ 80
ref: nc
teach: nc
---
q: connect to a telnet service
a: telnet @host@ @port@
ref: telnet
teach: telnet
---
q: telnet passing a chosen login name
a: telnet -l @user@ @host@
ref: telnet
teach: telnet -l
---
q: telnet setting the escape character
a: telnet -a @host@
ref: telnet
teach: telnet -a
---
q: fetch a file over tftp
a: tftp -g -r file.txt @host@
ref: tftp
teach: tftp -g
teach: tftp -r
---
q: upload a file over tftp
a: tftp -p -l @txt@ @host@
ref: tftp
teach: tftp -p
teach: tftp -l
---
q: fetch over tftp using a chosen block size
a: tftp -b 1024 -g -r file.txt @host@
ref: tftp
teach: tftp -b
---
q: fetch a file from an ftp server
a: ftpget @host@ local.txt remote.txt
ref: ftpget
teach: ftpget
---
q: fetch from ftp with a username and password
a: ftpget -u @user@ -p secret @host@ local.txt remote.txt
ref: ftpget
teach: ftpget -u
teach: ftpget -p
---
q: fetch from ftp on a non-standard port
a: ftpget -P @port@ @host@ local.txt remote.txt
ref: ftpget
teach: ftpget -P
---
q: continue an interrupted ftp download
a: ftpget -c @host@ local.txt remote.txt
ref: ftpget
teach: ftpget -c
---
q: upload a file to an ftp server
a: ftpput @host@ remote.txt @txt@
ref: ftpput
teach: ftpput
---
q: upload to ftp with credentials
a: ftpput -u @user@ -p secret @host@ remote.txt @txt@
ref: ftpput
teach: ftpput -u
teach: ftpput -p
---
q: upload to ftp on a non-standard port
a: ftpput -P @port@ @host@ remote.txt @txt@
ref: ftpput
teach: ftpput -P
---
q: ask for a dhcp lease on @iface@
a: udhcpc -i @iface@
ref: udhcpc
teach: udhcpc -i
---
q: get a lease and exit rather than staying resident
a: udhcpc -i @iface@ -q
ref: udhcpc
teach: udhcpc -q
---
q: try three times before giving up
a: udhcpc -i @iface@ -t 3
ref: udhcpc
teach: udhcpc -t
---
q: wait one second between attempts
a: udhcpc -i @iface@ -T 1
ref: udhcpc
teach: udhcpc -T
---
q: run in the foreground rather than backgrounding itself
a: udhcpc -i @iface@ -f
ref: udhcpc
teach: udhcpc -f
---
q: exit rather than keep retrying if no lease arrives
a: udhcpc -i @iface@ -n
ref: udhcpc
teach: udhcpc -n
---
q: run a chosen script when the lease is obtained
a: udhcpc -i @iface@ -s /usr/share/udhcpc/default.script
ref: udhcpc
teach: udhcpc -s
---
q: release the current lease on exit
a: udhcpc -i @iface@ -R
ref: udhcpc
teach: udhcpc -R
